    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanhao">Li Yuanhao</a> levied every man between 15 and 60, put as many as 370,000 under arms, promulgated the Tangut script in 1036 and in 1038 declared himself emperor of the Great Xia; after six years of war the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> recognised him and paid an annual tribute of 250,000 units of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a>.</li><li>For most of the 11th century child emperors reigned under empress dowagers and their clans, the Mocang and then two generations of the Liang; Empress Dowager Liang rode at the head of the cavalry against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> until she was poisoned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> assassins in 1099.</li><li>Western Xia pioneered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> with ceramic and wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a>, and under Emperor Renzong (1139–1193) founded schools, examinations and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanlin-academy">Hanlin Academy</a> and completed most of the Tangut Buddhist canon; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed the state so thoroughly that its history stayed obscure until the 20th century.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Auspicious Tantra of All-Reaching Union, a 449-page Tangut text found in the ruins of the Baisigou Square Pagoda in the Helan Mountains, is the earliest surviving book printed with wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a>; twelve Tangut titles printed with movable type survive today.</p></aside>
    </section>

