ho led armies in person, is poisoned by assassins from the Liao; the Song 'advance and fortify' campaign has built 40 forts across the Ordos.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="347.6" x2="347.6" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="347.6" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="347.6" y="164" text-anchor="middle">5</text><title>1124: Emperor Chongzong turns away the fugitive Liao emperor Tianzuo and declares himself a vassal of the Jurchen Jin.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="435.2" x2="435.2" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="435.2" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="435.2" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1147: Emperor Renzong institutes imperial examinations, after founding schools throughout the country and Confucian temples.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="675.2" x2="675.2" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="675.2" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="675.2" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1210: After the Mongol siege of Zhongxing, Emperor Xiangzong submits to Genghis Khan, giving him his daughter Chaka and a tribute of camels, falcons and textiles.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>September 1227: Emperor Mo surrenders after a six-month siege and is executed; the Mongols slaughter the capital's population and plunder the imperial tombs.</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1038 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1227 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1038</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanhao">Li Yuanhao</a> declares himself emperor of the Great Xia at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yinchuan">Xingqing</a>, taking the Tangut clan name Weiming and creating a Chinese-style bureaucracy.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1044</span><span class="rf-text">After victories at Sanchuan Pass and Haoshuichuan and the repulse of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> invasion of 100,000, Jingzong makes peace: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> recognise him and pay 250,000 units of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> a year.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1081</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> launch a five-pronged invasion while the Liang clan imprisons Emperor Huizong; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanzhou">Lanzhou</a> falls, but the Xia flood the Song camps by breaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> dikes.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1099</span><span class="rf-text">Empress Dowager Liang, who led armies in person, is poisoned by assassins from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> 'advance and fortify' campaign has built 40 forts across the Ordos.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1124</span><span class="rf-text">Emperor Chongzong turns away the fugitive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> emperor Tianzuo and declares himself a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1147</span><span class="rf-text">Emperor Renzong institutes imperial examinations, after founding schools throughout the country and Confucian temples.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1210</span><span class="rf-text">After the Mongol siege of Zhongxing, Emperor Xiangzong submits to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, giving him his daughter Chaka and a tribute of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>, falcons and textiles.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">September 1227</span><span class="rf-text">Emperor Mo surrenders after a six-month siege and is executed; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> slaughter the capital's population and plunder the imperial tombs.</span></li></ol>
